1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,784
HallSort checks everyday items against HKU's published re Kiosk rules.

2
00:00:06,154 --> 00:00:10,897
This is the final local app. The narration is synthetic.

3
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:17,241
In catalog mode, choosing the coffee cup set updates the input and character count.

4
00:00:17,611 --> 00:00:21,830
One check returns three parts, each with a source.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:29,023
The clean lid goes to plastic, the sleeve to paper, and the clean paper cup to beverage cartons.

6
00:00:29,393 --> 00:00:33,267
These categories come from the HKU Photo Guide.

7
00:00:33,637 --> 00:00:37,241
Now we add an unknown object to office paper.

8
00:00:37,611 --> 00:00:43,474
HallSort refuses the entire request, leaving the unknown part unclassified.

9
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:48,693
In AI mode, a lithium battery triggers a local safety check.

10
00:00:49,063 --> 00:00:53,717
The label says no model call, and the app assigns no bin.

11
00:00:54,087 --> 00:00:59,400
For an ordinary AI query, this recording uses a server with no key.

12
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:05,694
The app shows that AI mode is unavailable. Catalog mode still works.

13
00:01:06,064 --> 00:01:12,003
On October twenty-fifth, the full live rerun passed thirty-two curated cases.

14
00:01:12,373 --> 00:01:18,076
On November nineteenth, a new run stopped after two unavailable responses.

15
00:01:18,446 --> 00:01:25,159
On the final Windows build, twenty-six contract tests and thirty-six catalog cases passed.

16
00:01:25,529 --> 00:01:30,623
At a collection point, follow its posted signage and staff guidance.
